/P 639 0 R
/E (We use a compatibility matrix to make design decisions, which numerically rates our prototypes based on the qualities we want in that specific module. We first prototyped a catapult, but found it could only fire one ball in 1.3 seconds. Our single-flywheel prototype shot all 3 in under 1 second. Our direct driven shooter achieved a 0.3 second wind up time, but caused bounce-outs. The next iteration used a belted flywheel shooter, making it compact and eliminating bounce-outs.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
